Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Permission Denied for Packet Capture
If you encounter permission issues:

# Add user to wireshark group
sudo usermod -a -G wireshark $USER

# Set proper capabilities
sudo setcap cap_net_raw,cap_net_admin=eip /usr/bin/dumpcap

# Restart your session or use newgrp
newgrp wireshark
Issue 2: No Network Interface Available
If no interfaces are shown:

# Check available interfaces
ip link show

# Ensure interface is up
sudo ip link set eth0 up

# Check if interface supports monitor mode
iwconfig 2>/dev/null
Issue 3: Capture Files Not Generated
If capture files are empty or not created:

# Check disk space
df -h /tmp

# Verify network activity
ping -c 5 google.com

# Use verbose mode for debugging
sudo tshark -i eth0 -v -c 10
Issue 4: Analysis Scripts Not Working
If analysis scripts fail:

# Check if capture files exist
ls -la /tmp/*.pcap

# Verify tshark installation
which tshark

# Run scripts with error output
bash -x /tmp/analyze_dns.sh
